  "result": "Excellent! All 212 tests pass, including 14 new voucher tests. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**src/errors.js**\n- Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS`: \"Invoice already has a voucher applied.\"\n\n**src/invoices.js**\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n  - Include voucher amount in calculations (0 if no voucher)\n  - Return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n  - Calculate total as: `subtotal - discount + vat - voucher`\n  - Clamp final total to 0 (never negative)\n\n- Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` that:\n  - Validates invoice is in draft status (NOT_DRAFT if not)\n  - Prevents duplicate vouchers (VOUCHER_EXISTS if already applied)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID if not)\n  - Sets `invoice.voucher = { code, amount }`\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) without mutating original\n\n**Tests (14 total)**\n- invoiceTotals with/without vouchers, single/multiple lines\n- Clamping behavior (voucher can't make total negative)\n- applyVoucher validation (draft status, duplicate prevention, amount validation)\n- Immutability, integration with other features\n\nThe voucher system:\n- Works per-line calculation (VAT, discount) \u2192 per-invoice deduction (voucher)\n- One voucher per invoice maximum\n- Draft invoices only (prevent voucher changes after issue)\n- All amounts in integer cents\n\nAll 212 tests pass (198 previous + 14 new).",
